s","k":"landmark","la":17.532,"lo":-88.17,"d":4869,"ds":"The Bay settlement, earliest predecessor state of modern Belize, is commonly thought to have been surreptitiously founded by British buccaneers, who thereby became the first Baymen, in the 17th century, during the Spanish or Precolonial periods of the country's history.","wpu":"Founding of Belize","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/David_Cox_-_Pirate%27s_Isle_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/960px-David_Cox_-_Pirate%27s_Isle_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Belize City is the largest city in Belize. It was once the capital of the former British Honduras. According to the 2022 census, Belize City has a population of 63,999 people.","wpu":"Belize City","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Belize_City_Montage.jpeg/960px-Belize_City_Montage.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}